      "created_at": "2025-10-21T12:26:28.369Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hi <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/oussamac\">@oussamac</a></p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"oussamac\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"155797\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/user_avatar/discuss.frappe.io/oussamac/48/91470_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> oussamac:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I want this one:</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>This is new <code>develop</code> (upcoming <code>version-16</code>)</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"oussamac\" data-post=\"4\" data-topic=\"155797\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/user_avatar/discuss.frappe.io/oussamac/48/91470_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> oussamac:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The installation I’m doing using either the develop or version-15, I always get this:</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>This screenshot is <code>version-15</code> … maybe you are missing something on installing new version.</p>\n<p>Just to clarify … new UI is not built with Frappe UI library (Vue), just JS (as always …)<br>\nActually both follows same design pattern and styles. So apps developed with Frappe UI library and new v16 looks like similar.</p>\n<p>See this video from last Frappeverse</p>\n<div class=\"youtube-onebox lazy-video-container\" data-video-id=\"7RiSSUvAcEk\" data-video-title=\"New Framework Features in ERPNext v16 :Frappeverse 2025\" data-video-start-time=\"\" data-provider-name=\"youtube\">\n  <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7RiSSUvAcEk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"video-thumbnail\" rel=\"noopener\">\n    <img class=\"youtube-thumbnail\" src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/7RiSSUvAcEk/maxresdefault.jpg\" title=\"New Framework Features in ERPNext v16 :Frappeverse 2025\" width=\"690\" height=\"388\">\n  </a>\n</div>\n\n<p>Hope this helps.</p>",
